    {
      "case_id": "sgr-ingress-low-exposure",
      "platform": "terraform",
      "domain": "networking",
      "source": {
        "repo": "https://github.com/bridgecrewio/terragoat",
        "commit": "729f8da6",
        "path": "terraform/aws/db-app.tf"
      },
      "declared_context": {
        "aws_security_group_rule.ingress": {
          "sensitivity": 3,
          "criticality": 3
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "findings": [
          {
            "resource_identity": "aws_security_group_rule.ingress",
            "issue_class": "networking-config-hygiene",
            "unresolved_factors": [
              "exposure"
            ],
            "excluded_from_quality_claims": true
          }
        ],
        "notes": "aws_security_group_rule.ingress is declared in db-app.tf:136-143. Its cidr_blocks value at db-app.tf:141 is `cidr_blocks = [\"${aws_vpc.web_vpc.cidr_block}\"]` - a reference to another resource's attribute, not a literal CIDR. The bounded extractor's closed list of exposure patterns is literals-only (design spec section 3 / CLAUDE.md's context- extraction layer), so Public Exposure cannot be resolved for this finding from the IaC alone; it is recorded unresolved rather than defaulted to low. Measured over real adapter output: checkov CKV_AWS_23, trivy AWS-0124, tfsec AVD-AWS-0124, all mapping to networking-config-hygiene - no ingress-exposure class is emitted for this resource by any of the three scanners, so the unresolved state is carried purely as context, not asserted as a scanner finding this case does not have."
      }
    },
